# DNA-AND content · minerals and what each kind of ground is made of
# researched: standard mineralogy (mineral formulas as in mineral reference tables); crust make-up from geology
#   references (Earth's continental crust is mostly feldspars and quartz, with pyroxene, clays, micas, calcite and
#   iron oxides; basalt is mostly pyroxene, calcic plagioclase and olivine; the Moon's highlands are anorthite-rich,
#   its seas basalt with ilmenite; Mars's dust is basalt minerals reddened by hematite; icy worlds are water ice with
#   frozen carbon dioxide, nitrogen and methane). Shares are rough parts per 100 of the grains.
# Each grain of ground is one mineral, picked from its ground's mix; zooming into it shows that mineral's own atoms.
# grain-mm: the grains' sizes across, smallest to largest (Wentworth scale: sand 0.0625 to 2 mm, silt 0.0039 to 0.0625 mm,
#   clay below 0.0039 mm; dune sand mostly 0.2 to 0.5 mm; the Moon's dust about 0.04 to 0.1 mm; snow grains 0.1 to 2 mm).
# Crystal faces step down in single layers about 0.2 to 0.3 nm high, with flat terraces between usually 10 to 100 nm wide.
# atoms: the formula's atoms written out one by one (its real ratio); colour: the grain's colour as seen (0 to 1).
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · content/elements.dnat · content/geology.dnat

@mineral quartz
name: Quartz
formula: SiO2
atoms: Si O O
colour: 0.86 0.82 0.74

@mineral albite
name: Albite (sodium feldspar)
formula: NaAlSi3O8
atoms: Na Al Si Si Si O O O O O O O O
colour: 0.9 0.88 0.84

@mineral orthoclase
name: Orthoclase (potassium feldspar)
formula: KAlSi3O8
atoms: K Al Si Si Si O O O O O O O O
colour: 0.88 0.7 0.62

@mineral anorthite
name: Anorthite (calcium feldspar)
formula: CaAl2Si2O8
atoms: Ca Al Al Si Si O O O O O O O O
colour: 0.82 0.82 0.8

@mineral forsterite
name: Olivine (forsterite)
formula: Mg2SiO4
atoms: Mg Mg Si O O O O
colour: 0.55 0.66 0.3

@mineral fayalite
name: Olivine (fayalite)
formula: Fe2SiO4
atoms: Fe Fe Si O O O O
colour: 0.42 0.38 0.2

@mineral enstatite
name: Pyroxene (enstatite)
formula: MgSiO3
atoms: Mg Si O O O
colour: 0.4 0.38 0.3

@mineral augite
name: Pyroxene (augite)
formula: CaMgSi2O6
atoms: Ca Mg Si Si O O O O O O
colour: 0.22 0.22 0.2

@mineral kaolinite
name: Clay (kaolinite)
formula: Al2Si2O5(OH)4
atoms: Al Al Si Si O O O O O O O O O H H H H
colour: 0.84 0.78 0.66

@mineral biotite
name: Mica (biotite)
formula: KMg3AlSi3O10(OH)2
atoms: K Mg Mg Mg Al Si Si Si O O O O O O O O O O O O H H
colour: 0.25 0.2 0.14

@mineral calcite
name: Calcite
formula: CaCO3
atoms: Ca C O O O
colour: 0.94 0.92 0.86

@mineral hematite
name: Hematite
formula: Fe2O3
atoms: Fe Fe O O O
colour: 0.6 0.22 0.14

@mineral magnetite
name: Magnetite
formula: Fe3O4
atoms: Fe Fe Fe O O O O
colour: 0.16 0.16 0.17

@mineral ilmenite
name: Ilmenite
formula: FeTiO3
atoms: Fe Ti O O O
colour: 0.18 0.17 0.17

@mineral pyrite
name: Pyrite
formula: FeS2
atoms: Fe S S
colour: 0.8 0.7 0.36

@mineral gypsum
name: Gypsum
formula: CaSO4·2H2O
atoms: Ca S O O O O O O H H H H
colour: 0.95 0.94 0.9

@mineral halite
name: Halite (rock salt)
formula: NaCl
atoms: Na Cl
colour: 0.95 0.93 0.93

@mineral sulfur
name: Sulfur
formula: S8
atoms: S S S S S S S S
colour: 0.92 0.84 0.2

@mineral water-ice
name: Water ice
formula: H2O
atoms: O H H
colour: 0.88 0.93 0.98

@mineral sea-water
name: Sea water
formula: H2O with dissolved salt
atoms: O H H O H H O H H O H H O H H O H H O H H O H H O H H Na Cl
colour: 0.2 0.4 0.6

@mineral dry-ice
name: Carbon dioxide ice
formula: CO2
atoms: C O O
colour: 0.94 0.94 0.94

@mineral nitrogen-ice
name: Nitrogen ice
formula: N2
atoms: N N
colour: 0.92 0.88 0.86

@mineral methane-ice
name: Methane ice
formula: CH4
atoms: C H H H H
colour: 0.82 0.74 0.66

# ── what each kind of ground is made of: mineral share, mineral share, ... (parts per 100) ──

@mix temperate
name: Land of a temperate world
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
minerals: quartz 25, albite 18, orthoclase 14, kaolinite 12, augite 6, biotite 5, calcite 8, hematite 5, magnetite 3, forsterite 2, gypsum 2

@mix desert
name: Dry rocky ground
grain-mm: 0.2..0.5
minerals: quartz 22, hematite 14, albite 14, augite 14, forsterite 10, enstatite 6, magnetite 6, gypsum 6, halite 4, calcite 4

@mix lava
name: Fresh basalt and lava rock
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: augite 28, anorthite 26, forsterite 18, fayalite 6, magnetite 10, ilmenite 6, sulfur 4, pyrite 2

@mix snowball
name: Frozen ground
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: water-ice 70, dry-ice 10, nitrogen-ice 5, methane-ice 5, forsterite 5, enstatite 5

@mix moon
name: Moon ground
grain-mm: 0.04..0.1
minerals: anorthite 40, augite 22, forsterite 14, ilmenite 14, fayalite 5, quartz 5

@mix tidally-locked
name: Ground of a tidally locked world
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
minerals: augite 22, anorthite 18, quartz 14, hematite 14, forsterite 12, water-ice 10, magnetite 10

@mix ocean
name: Sea floor
grain-mm: 0.01..0.06
minerals: augite 30, anorthite 25, forsterite 15, calcite 15, kaolinite 10, pyrite 5

@mix sea
name: The sea
grain-mm: 0..0
minerals: sea-water 100

@mix ice
name: Sea ice and ice sheets
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: water-ice 100
